  "answer": "I'll check the workspace structure first, then create the file.\nCreated `src/unit.ts`:\n\n```ts\nexport const unit = 21;\n```\n\nNotes:\n- The `src/` directory didn't exist, so I created it (`mkdir -p src`) before writing the file.\n- Nothing else was touched — `AGENTS.md` and `package.json` are unchanged, and no config or test-runner changes were made.\nCreated `src/double.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport { unit } from './unit';\n\nexport function double(): number {\n  return unit * 2;\n}\n```\n\nOnly `src/double.ts` was added; `src/unit.ts`, `AGENTS.md`, and `package.json` are untouched.\n\nOne thing to flag (no change made): `package.json` has `\"type\": \"module\"`, so under plain Node ESM the extension-less specifier `'./unit'` won't resolve at runtime — it would need `'./unit.js'` (or `'./unit.ts'` with a TS-aware loader). I used `'./unit'` exactly as you specified; say the word if you'd like the extension added.\nCreated `test/long.test.ts` and ran it — it passes and prints the exact marker.\n\n**File added** (`test/long.test.ts`):\n\n```ts\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport test from 'node:test';\n\nimport { double } from '../src/double.ts';\n\ntest('double() returns 42', () => {\n  assert.equal(double(), 42);\n  console.log('LONG_SESSION_OK');\n});\n```\n\nThe marker is printed inside the test body *after* the assertion, so it can only appear when the assertion holds.\n\n**Run results**\n\n`bun test test/long.test.ts`:\n```\ntest/long.test.ts:\nLONG_SESSION_OK\n(pass) double() returns 42 [0.09ms]\n 1 pass\n 0 fail\n```\n\n`node --test` (spec reporter) also passes: `✔ double() returns 42`, `ℹ pass 1 / ℹ fail 0`, with `LONG_SESSION_OK` on its own line. Note that this Node run needed a one-off, in-memory resolution shim on the command line (nothing written to the repo), because plain `node --test test/long.test.ts` fails with:\n\n```\nERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND: Cannot find module '.../src/unit' imported from .../src/double.ts\n```\n\nThat is the caveat I flagged earlier coming due: `package.json` has `\"type\": \"module\"`, and `src/double.ts` imports `'./unit'` without an extension exactly as you specified, which Node's ESM resolver rejects. Nothing else in the workspace was changed — `AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, `src/unit.ts`, and `src/double.ts` are byte-identical to before, and no config files or dependencies were added.\n\nIf you want `node --test test/long.test.ts` to work unaided, the single-line fix is changing `'./unit'` to `'./unit.ts'` in `src/double.ts` (Node-type-stripping friendly; `'./unit.js'` won't work since Node doesn't remap `.js`→`.ts`). I left it alone because you explicitly asked for `'./unit'` — say the word and I'll make that change.\nThe test does fail under the default Node runner (`node --test`) — not an assertion failure but `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND` from `src/double.ts` importing extension-less `'./unit'`. That's a source-file defect, so I'll repair the source (not the test) and re-run.\nThe test was failing under the default Node runner, so I repaired the source and re-ran. It now passes on both runners.\n\n**Diagnosis.** `node --test test/long.test.ts` reported `pass 0 / fail 1`, but the failure was never the assertion — it was `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND: Cannot find module '.../src/unit' imported from .../src/double.ts`. `package.json` declares `\"type\": \"module\"`, and Node's ESM resolver does not do extension guessing, so the extension-less specifier in `src/double.ts` broke module linking before `double()` could even be called. The test file itself was correct and was left untouched (its SHA-256 is still `c2dc0bfb…`).\n\n**Repair (source only, one line):**\n\n```diff\n- import { unit } from './unit';\n+ import { unit } from './unit.ts';\n```\n\nI chose `'./unit.ts'` over `'./unit.js'` because Node's type stripping does not remap `.js` → `.ts`, so `'./unit.js'` would still fail. `src/unit.ts` is unchanged (`ef308ad7…`), and `AGENTS.md` / `package.json` are byte-identical to before; no config, no dependencies, no runner changes, and `test/long.test.ts` was not edited.\n\n**Re-run — `node --test --test-reporter=spec test/long.test.ts`, exit 0:**\n```\nLONG_SESSION_OK\n✔ double() returns 42 (0.592375ms)\nℹ tests 1\nℹ pass 1\nℹ fail 0\n```\n\n**Also green under `bun test test/long.test.ts`:**\n```\nLONG_SESSION_OK\n(pass) double() returns 42 [0.10ms]\n 1 pass\n 0 fail\n```\n\nThe marker appears on its own line, and only after the assertion holds.\n\nOne tradeoff worth knowing: `'./unit.ts'` is what lets plain Node run this unassisted, but a `tsc` check would flag it (TS5097) unless `allowImportingTsExtensions` is enabled — and I can't add a config file here. Since this project has no build/typecheck step and no configured runner, Node correctness is the useful property; if you later add `tsconfig.json` with that flag, everything stays consistent.\n**Files created**\n\n| File | Status | Contents |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/unit.ts` | created, unchanged since | `export const unit = 21;` |\n| `src/double.ts` | created, then repaired (one line) | `import { unit } from './unit.ts';` + `export function double(): number { return unit * 2; }` |\n| `test/long.test.ts` | created, never edited | imports `node:test`/`node:assert/strict` and `double` from `'../src/double.ts'`; asserts `double() === 42`, then logs the marker |\n\nNot touched: `AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, `test/oracle.test.ts` (not present in the workspace), no config files, no dependencies, no runner changes.\n\nThe only modification to an existing file was in `src/double.ts`, changing `'./unit'` → `'./unit.ts'` so Node's ESM resolver could link the module; the test file itself was never altered.\n\n**Exact printed marker:**\n\n```\nLONG_SESSION_OK\n```"
